Architecture follows the established Apple precedent (BatteryRadialGauge dashboard
widget): a thin @Observable model injects the shared-core store and republishes
its cache-then-network Resource<FeedbackListResponse> as a LoadableState; ALL
display logic lives in pure, KMP-free value types so the whole surface is unit
tested without the live graph. Hooks ported keep the web names at the Swift call
sites:
  useFeedbackList   -> FeedbackQueuePageModel.rebind() -> store.feedbackList(params:)   (GET /admin/feedback{buildQuery})
  useUpdateFeedback -> updateStatus/saveGithubURL/forwardToGithub -> store.updateFeedback (PATCH /admin/feedback/{id})

