Note on Swift 6.3.2: an IRGen reabstraction-thunk compiler crash
(llvm::report_fatal_error on @$s9TeslaSync18FeedbackStatusKind...TR) was triggered
by SwiftUI Picker-over-custom-enum selection + Task closures under
SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY=complete. Worked around WITHOUT losing parity: the three
selectors bind String rawValues (mapping String<->enum at the edge) and Task
lifetimes moved into the model. Type-checking always passed; codegen now succeeds.

